France introduced a mandatory durability index replacing the repairability index for electronics and appliances, displaying a 0-10 reliability and reparability rating. Starting January 2024 for televisions and April 2024 for washing machines, the system scores products by availability of technical documentation, spare parts accessibility, disassembly ease, and upgrade possibilities. The index empowers consumers to make informed purchasing decisions by showing environmental lifecycle impact and long-term value, driving manufacturers to design for longevity rather than disposability.